{"/api/discogs/artist/24088/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"24088","image":"https://i.discogs.com/2SfwK2TXdnPiUxtE2-xJ8ZrHWeQ4JehjbeeRd2G_H5Y/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI0MDg4/LTE2ODMzNTIwMzUt/ODE1MC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/D9lOS8EnkNsrpUgFOhl6pVcSscBpEMOXMtz4qQ7kndU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI0MDg4/LTE2ODMzNTIwMzUt/ODE1MC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Few individuals can claim to have done so much for musical exchange across the globe as Berlin based DJ, producer and label boss Daniel Haaksman. With the release of his 2004 compilation \"Rio Baile Funk Favela Booty Beats\" he introduced the sound of Rio ́s favelas for the first time to a global audience, parallely creating the genre term „Baile Funk“ (in Brasil, the music is called „Funk Carioca“).\r\n\r\nFrom 2005 Daniel gave the sound of Rio De Janeiro its own platform and the Berlin treatment and started Man Recordings, today considered one of the leading international labels in tropical bass music. Man Recordings has released countless records by artists such as such as Diplo, Schlachthofbronx, Crookers, Bert On Beats or Daniel Haaksman himself amongst others, as well as the creme of Brazilian artists such as Deize Tigrona, Mulú, Cibelle, Edu K, MC Tha, João Brasil, Lovefoxxx or Marina Gasolina.\r\n\r\nDaniel ́s own musical output includes four albums (\"Rambazamba\" (2010), \"African Fabrics\" (2016), With Love, From Berlin\" (2019), \"Sonido Lava\" (2023),  as well as other compilations such as \"Bossa Do Morro\" on Universal Germany (2008), \"Tecno Brega\" on Man Recordings (2010), \"Black Atlantica Edits\" on BBE (2020) as well as official remixes for artists such as Gotan Project, Dom Salvador E Abolição, Lord Nelson or Pinduca amongst others. As a DJ, he has travelled the world and played numerous clubs, festivals and events, such as Glastonbury, Womad or Tim Festival. His party friendly mix of baile funk, house, trap, bubbling, kuduro and everything in between has excited audiences everywhere. Daniel knows no musical rules, except for one: A DJ has to rock the party.\r\n\r\nFrom 2013 to 2016 Daniel hosted the weekly radio mix show „Luso FM“ on German public radio „WDR Funkhaus Europa“. He also writes as a freelance music journalist for various German language dailies and weeklies. \r\n\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:24088","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":437920,"name":"Haaksman & Haaksman"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["D. Haaksman","D. Haaksmen","DJ Haaksman","Haaksman"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/24088-Daniel-Haaksman","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.danielhaaksman.com","http://www.instagram.com/danielhaaksman","http://www.facebook.com/DANIELHAAKSMAN","http://www.soundcloud.com/daniel-haaksman","http://www.manrecordings.com"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2923672/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2923672","image":"https://i.discogs.com/McitfSF3NpimHb_25N6eDrWaEhY7E7XiKGQ_jWUkeIs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:597/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5MjM2/NzItMTQ2MjAzNzUy/Mi02OTY1LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/w6FwUgMVwc4L4Md_895q-Y4CdqHt3SKoTYGf5EWWkK8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5MjM2/NzItMTQ2MjAzNzUy/Mi02OTY1LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Prolific Ecuadorian accordionist, organist, poet and composer born in 1944 in the city of Ambato. A pioneer of the Moog synthesizer in Tropical music. Former director and producer at the label [l=Fadisa]. He is the composer of songs such as La Minga, El Camote, Casita De Pobres, Pañuelo De Seda, Agua Loca, Ponchito De colores, Cumbia Triste, and Pepe Chupín. He currently lives in the United States.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2923672","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":4903986,"name":"Lupe Meléndez"},{"id":5118039,"name":"Junior Y Su Equipo"},{"id":5736728,"name":"Luis Edén"},{"id":13395729,"name":"Carlos Palmerito"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":5023949,"name":"Conjunto Los Chagras Quiteños"},{"active":true,"id":5031794,"name":"Olmedo Torres Y Su Cuarteto"},{"active":true,"id":5184506,"name":"Los Locos Del Ritmo (2)"},{"active":true,"id":5197802,"name":"Conjunto Combo Puruha"},{"active":true,"id":5212323,"name":"El Combo Mayorga"},{"active":true,"id":5556006,"name":"Quinteto Casino"},{"active":true,"id":5847933,"name":"Grupo 5 (3)"},{"active":true,"id":5886953,"name":"Conjunto De Polibio Mayorga"},{"active":true,"id":5937613,"name":"Polibio Mayorga Y Su Sonora"},{"active":true,"id":6289999,"name":"Conjunto Siboney (2)"},{"active":true,"id":6926042,"name":"Coro Música Libre"},{"active":true,"id":7244040,"name":"Los Sinfonicos (2)"},{"active":true,"id":13391838,"name":"Polibio Mayorga Y Su Orquesta"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Conj. Polibio Mayorga","Conjunto De Polibio Mayorga","Conjunto Hamelyn","Conjunto Popular De Teresita","Los Guambras","Luis Polibio Mayorga","Lupe Meléndez","Mayorga","P. M.","P. Mayorga","P. Mayorga y su Acordeón","P. Moreyra","P.Mayorga","Polibin Mayorga","Polibio Mayorga Organo y Ritmo","Polibio Mayorga Organo y Ritmos","Polibio Mayorga Su Organo Y Ritmos","Polibio Mayorga Sus Violines Y Ritmos","Polibio Mayorga Y Conjunto Rítmico","Polibio Mayorga Y Su Acordeón","Polibio Mayorga Y Su Conjunto","Polibio Mayorga Y Su Organo","Polibio Mayorga Y Sus Amigos","Polibio Y Su Vibrafono","Polibo Mayorga","Polivio Mallorga","Polivio Mayorga","Taller De Música","Taller de Música"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2923672-Polibio-Mayorga","type":"artist","urls":["https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polibio_Mayorga","https://www.facebook.com/Polibio-Mayorga-140261739341367/","https://www.facebook.com/polibio.mayorga?ref=br_rs","https://open.spotify.com/artist/1zjOtZAqIcwJVMmKOoB60K?si=2Wdcxb76Q7e5qzXqR7UDqQ"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2929902/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2929902","image":"https://i.discogs.com/dWLMnGTQ03WyQfJqJ4skVhDs7zJbB-aQbhiqctfEhQ8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:535/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5Mjk5/MDItMTczNDM2OTYy/My04NDAyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/NI0MbJX7sj3uW-69PtTUT0zd2Rqf-jMhRg1QXMLusIU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5Mjk5/MDItMTczNDM2OTYy/My04NDAyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Farruko is a reggaeton and Latin pop singer from Puerto Rico. His given name is Carlos Efren Reyes, and he was born in Bayamon, Puerto Rico in 1991. At the age of 16, he began to post his songs under his stage name to MySpace. His first single, \"Sexo Fuera del Planeta,\" gained thousands of followers, and from there he explored the potential of other social media networks. Due to his massive success on the Internet, he came to the attention of Puerto Rican radio and music industry executives, who enlisted his vocal talents for other artists.\r\nFarruko's debut album, El Talento del Bloque, appeared when he was 18. It was released by Siente Music and distributed by Universal. Most of its 13 songs were self-penned. The set became an almost instant hit, and several singles followed from it. Some of the album's highlights included its collaborative tunes such as \"Su Hija Me Gusta\" with José Feliciano, \"Ella No Es Facil\" with Cosculluela, and \"Traime a Tu Amiga\" with Arcangel and Julio Voltio. He also issued the non-album smash \"Pa Romper la Discoteca\" with Daddy Yankee and Yomo. \r\nIn 2012, he issued his sophomore offering, TMPR: The Most Powerful Rookie. Its first smash single was \"Feel the Rhythm\" (\"Siente el Ritmo\"), though it was one of five. As a whole, the set demonstrated that Farruko was as comfortable in electro and pop circles as he was in reggaeton; it was nominated for a Latin Grammy.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2929902","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":5817362,"name":"Carlos Efrén Reyes Rosado"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Farruco","Farruko Reggaeton"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2929902-Farruko","type":"artist","urls":["https://farruko.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3548464/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3548464","image":"https://i.discogs.com/N5fQNJ0kj95FW1hTvaUhNM5ekw4NTzwsSWf8zDl2xRo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:380/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM1NDg0/NjQtMTU0MTg1NTI4/Ni00MTgyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/PZ0ijdHg3dvou6P-XqgV0Tl9u5QSvLBkhWnp3NpdfMA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM1NDg0/NjQtMTU0MTg1NTI4/Ni00MTgyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Brazilian rapper.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3548464","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Karol Conká"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3548464-Karol-Conka","type":"artist","urls":["http://karolconka.com","https://www.facebook.com/karolconka","https://twitter.com/karolconka","https://www.youtube.com/user/karolconka","https://www.instagram.com/karolconka","https://soundcloud.com/karolconka","https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karol_Conka"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/3879/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3879","image":"https://i.discogs.com/V9VYQVy0z6zMfASt1xwEclDBwAfbEFuTMHIQKX4eOoM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:400/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM4Nzkt/MTYyNjk0NDAwOS0y/MjA2LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/tkivMoAYXatOKONBEoIUXacTN_8TgrriCRJMf05tsAg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM4Nzkt/MTYyNjk0NDAwOS0y/MjA2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Japanese guitarist, musician, audio / video artist. Born January 27, 1969 in Setagaya-ku, Tokyo. He was married to [a=Takako Minekawa] from 2000 to 2012. He is a second cousin to [a=Miki Berenyi] and Joi Ito.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3879","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":32061,"name":"Keigo Oyamada"},{"id":91807